From: p5r-proton
Subject: ntdll: restore Wine 7 CPU topology override handling

Proton 8 moved to a Wine 8 base and Persona 5 Royal regressed from being
GPU-bound to CPU-bound with low CPU/GPU utilisation.  As a targeted
experiment, restore the Wine 7 CPU topology behaviour while keeping the
modern Wine base:

- WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY requires an explicit logical count and host CPU map
  again; Wine 11's automatic "pick N CPUs" and hybrid performance-core
  ("P" prefix) selection are removed.
- The SMT override is tracked with Wine 7's single boolean instead of
  per-CPU thread sibling masks.
- RelationProcessorCore entries always report EfficiencyClass 0, as Wine 7
  did, instead of deriving it from /sys/devices/cpu_core.

The generic (non-override) CPU enumeration path is left untouched.
